6. ⚡ OPTIMIZATION & BEST PRACTICES
🚨 Mistake #1

Forget WHERE.

UPDATE Books

SET Price=100;

What happens?

Every book becomes ₹100.

This has happened in real companies.

Correct:

UPDATE Books

SET Price=100

WHERE BookID=101;
🚨 Mistake #2

Delete everything.

DELETE FROM Books;

No WHERE.

Every row gone.

Correct:

DELETE FROM Books

WHERE BookID=101;
🚨 Mistake #3

Wrong INSERT order.

Suppose table:

BookID

BookName

Price

Wrong:

INSERT INTO Books

VALUES

('DBMS',499,101);

Types won't match.

Senior Engineer Habit

Before UPDATE or DELETE:

Always run:

SELECT *
FROM Books
WHERE BookID=101;

Confirm the correct row.

Then execute UPDATE or DELETE.

Professionals do this constantly.
